# Copy to .dev.vars for local development:  cp .dev.vars.example .dev.vars
#
# The allowlist is fail-closed: a chain that is not listed here is rejected,
# and an empty list serves nobody. There is no accept-everything mode — it
# would be one stray var away from letting any chain on the internet spawn a
# Durable Object on the deployed worker.
#
# To watch your own node, put its genesis hash in TELEMETRY_CHAINS. Read it
# from the running node:
#
#   curl -s -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
#     -d '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"chain_getBlockHash","params":[0]}' \
#     http://localhost:9944
#
# `--dev` mints a fresh genesis on every restart, so that hash changes whenever
# you wipe the chain; paste the new one and restart `wrangler dev`. Running
# against a persistent local chain (`--chain local`, a fixed base path) avoids
# the churn.
TELEMETRY_CHAINS=

# wrangler dev reads this file and it overrides the `vars` block in
# wrangler.jsonc, which holds the real testnet hash for production. Set this to
# watch the live testnet from a local worker instead of your own chain.
TELEMETRY_TESTNET_GENESIS=
TELEMETRY_MAINNET_GENESIS=
